{"type":"assistant","uuid":"620ddf82-a25c-464f-adda-b63ade88de97","session_id":"e9011526-0d5e-4971-8e20-3a82ef4b0828","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"id":"620ddf82-a25c-464f-adda-b63ade88de97","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n\n## Summary\n\n**Bug:** Negative Credits — Players could place towers even when they had insufficient credits, causing their credit balance to go below zero.\n\n**Root Cause:** In `ScoreBoard.takeCredits()`, credits were subtracted without any lower-bound check:\n```java\n// Before (buggy)\npublic synchronized void takeCredits(int credits) {\n    mCredits -= credits;\n    creditsChanged();\n}\n```\n\n**Fix:** Added a `Math.max(0, ...)` clamp in `ScoreBoard.takeCredits()` to ensure credits never go below zero:\n```java\n// After (fixed)\npublic synchronized void takeCredits(int credits) {\n    mCredits = Math.max(0, mCredits - credits);\n    creditsChanged();\n}\n```\n\n**Why this location:** `takeCredits()` is the single point where credits are deducted — called from tower purchase (`TowerInserter`), tower upgrades (`TowerControl`), and tower enhancements. Clamping here handles all credit-spending paths in one place, preventing negative credits everywhere.\n\n**File modified:** `app/src/main/java/ch/logixisland/anuto/business/score/ScoreBoard.java` (line 45-46)"}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":34962,"output_tokens":272,"cache_read_input_tokens":33536,"total_tokens":35234}}}
