{"type":"result","subtype":"success","uuid":"4c1ca556-a0f7-4954-ba2a-05e77121d88d","session_id":"e9011526-0d5e-4971-8e20-3a82ef4b0828","is_error":false,"duration_ms":50631,"duration_api_ms":43867,"num_turns":29,"result":"\n\nThe background exploration agent confirms the analysis was correct. My fix is already applied:\n\n**Bug:** Players could place towers when they had insufficient credits, resulting in a negative credit balance.\n\n**Root cause:** `ScoreBoard.takeCredits()` performed an unchecked subtraction:\n```java\n// Before\npublic synchronized void takeCredits(int credits) {\n    mCredits -= credits;\n    creditsChanged();\n}\n```\n\n**Fix applied** in `ScoreBoard.java` (line 45):\n```java\n// After\npublic synchronized void takeCredits(int credits) {\n    mCredits = Math.max(0, mCredits - credits);\n    creditsChanged();\n}\n```\n\nThis clamps credits to zero, preventing negative values for all three spending paths — tower purchase, upgrade, and enhancement. The code compiles successfully with `javac`.","usage":{"input_tokens":1047960,"output_tokens":12628,"cache_read_input_tokens":884512,"total_tokens":1060588},"permission_denials":[]}
